The fourth charge is why this isn't just

273
00:10:11,651 --> 00:10:12,860
another tunnel case.

274
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:16,679
On February 20, 2025, the United States

275
00:10:16,679 --> 00:10:20,848
designated CJNG a foreign terrorist organization.

276
00:10:21,848 --> 00:10:24,330
It wasn't the first time prosecutors took that

277
00:10:24,330 --> 00:10:26,111
approach against the same cartel.

278
00:10:26,111 --> 00:10:28,594
In May 2025, in the Western District of Texas,

279
00:10:28,594 --> 00:10:31,022
the Justice Department unsealed an indictment

280
00:10:31,022 --> 00:10:33,451
alleging that a Mexican national conspired to

281
00:10:33,451 --> 00:10:35,933
provide grenades to CJNG The department called

282
00:10:35,933 --> 00:10:38,416
it the first in the nation to charge a Mexican

283
00:10:38,416 --> 00:10:40,898
national with material support to a designated

284
00:10:40,898 --> 00:10:43,003
foreign terrorist organization based on

285
00:10:43,003 --> 00:10:44,568
involvement with that cartel.

286
00:10:45,468 --> 00:10:46,922
That case alleged weapons.

287
00:10:46,922 --> 00:10:48,376
This one alleges a tunnel.

288
00:10:48,376 --> 00:10:50,892
The announcement doesn't say whether it's the

289
00:10:50,892 --> 00:10:52,849
first tunnel case charged this way.

290
00:10:53,849 --> 00:10:55,705
Five dates frame the case.

291
00:10:56,705 --> 00:11:00,295
The statute for the terrorism charge is 18 U.S.C.

292
00:11:00,295 --> 00:11:00,735
2339B.

293
00:11:00,735 --> 00:11:03,812
Providing material support to a designated

294
00:11:03,812 --> 00:11:07,036
foreign terrorist organization. The maximum:

295
00:11:07,036 --> 00:11:09,527
twenty years, and a $500,000 fine.

296
00:11:10,427 --> 00:11:12,153
Look at the arithmetic, though.

297
00:11:12,153 --> 00:11:14,547
The terrorism count carries a lower maximum

298
00:11:14,547 --> 00:11:16,051
than the two import counts.

299
00:11:16,051 --> 00:11:16,997
Those carry life.

300
00:11:17,997 --> 00:11:19,616
So what does the new count add?

301
00:11:19,616 --> 00:11:21,965
The announcement ties it to the same conduct,

302
00:11:21,965 --> 00:11:24,523
designing and building the tunnel for the cartel.

303
00:11:24,523 --> 00:11:26,403
It doesn't spell out more than that.

304
00:11:27,303 --> 00:11:29,799
Whether that conduct qualifies as material

305
00:11:29,799 --> 00:11:32,117
support is the kind of question defense

306
00:11:32,117 --> 00:11:33,900
lawyers and judges will argue.

307
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:35,921
Nothing about it has been decided.

308
00:11:37,021 --> 00:11:40,374
On the other side is what the complaint describes.

309
00:11:40,374 --> 00:11:42,586
A store with almost no customers.

310
00:11:42,586 --> 00:11:44,531
Three vehicles. 851 packages.

311
00:11:45,531 --> 00:11:48,005
Which leaves what nobody has answered yet.

312
00:11:48,505 --> 00:11:51,075
The Justice Department says the investigation

313
00:11:51,075 --> 00:11:51,703
is ongoing.

314
00:11:51,703 --> 00:11:54,273
Six people besides him have been charged, and

315
00:11:54,273 --> 00:11:55,758
only four have been named.

316
00:11:55,758 --> 00:11:57,871
Whether more are coming isn't public.

317
00:11:58,671 --> 00:12:00,083
Then there's detection.

318
00:12:00,083 --> 00:12:02,662
A 2025 Homeland Security inspector general

319
00:12:02,662 --> 00:12:05,487
audit, as we understand it, found that Customs

320
00:12:05,487 --> 00:12:08,066
and Border Protection was still evaluating

321
00:12:08,066 --> 00:12:09,785
tunnel detection technology.

322
00:12:10,585 --> 00:12:12,127
That's the part that sticks.

323
00:12:12,127 --> 00:12:14,604
This tunnel came out because somebody watched

324
00:12:14,604 --> 00:12:16,421
a loading routine for six months.

325
00:12:16,421 --> 00:12:18,457
Nothing public says a machine saw it.

326
00:12:19,457 --> 00:12:20,715
Three questions remain.

327
00:12:20,715 --> 00:12:23,067
Whether he is brought to the United States.

328
00:12:23,067 --> 00:12:25,310
Whether the other two defendants are ever

329
00:12:25,310 --> 00:12:25,912
identified.

330
00:12:25,912 --> 00:12:28,209
And whether a court agrees that building a

331
00:12:28,209 --> 00:12:30,999
tunnel for a cartel counts as supporting terrorism.

332
00:12:32,099 --> 00:12:34,441
For now, here is what the record shows.

333
00:12:34,441 --> 00:12:36,603
A tunnel under a store in Otay Mesa.

334
00:12:36,603 --> 00:12:38,225
More than a ton of cocaine.

335
00:12:38,225 --> 00:12:40,627
And a grand jury that says a 60-year-old

336
00:12:40,627 --> 00:12:43,149
engineer from Guadalajara helped build it.

337
00:12:44,149 --> 00:12:45,774
He has not been convicted.

338
00:12:45,774 --> 00:12:48,585
A grand jury has accused him, and a judge has

339
00:12:48,585 --> 00:12:49,585
decided nothing.

340
00:12:49,585 --> 00:12:52,021
Under the law, he is presumed innocent.

341
00:12:53,221 --> 00:12:54,534
That's case file 025.

342
00:12:54,534 --> 00:12:57,284
If you want the history of the tunnels under

343
00:12:57,284 --> 00:13:00,222
this border, case file 002 is next on the list.

344
00:13:00,222 --> 00:13:03,097
And tell us in the comments, what should count

345
00:13:03,097 --> 00:13:03,909
as terrorism?
